Are you playing as root? don't - create a account in group users and
login with that when you play nethack. In your (either) /etc/profile  -
the NETHACKOPTIONS= line or in your ~/.nethackrc try seeing if changing
the option "checkpoint" - talked about in the guidebook makes a
difference. Other than that, it sounds to me like somebody fouled up the
compile. Try getting the precompiled version from the nethack developers
at: 

http://www.nethack.org/v343/ports/download-linux.html

The QT (tiled version you've probably been paying), the X11 - using
X11R6 builtin graphics and the tty - read ascii versions are all there.
If you have not luck with that, you would have to compile it yourself -
although I can't see it going to that extent, make sure you're not
destroying, killing, endtasking, or endtasking it's parent first though
- also that there is'nt a problem with a script which may run
/usr/lib/nethack - which is a script itself, so that's kind of unlikely.

